<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>03 · THE QUESTION</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 36, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        One question, and why it deserves a clean test
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Box style={{ marginTop: 26, padding: '24px 28px', background: '#16233A', borderLeft: '3px solid #4D8DFF' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 29, color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.4 }}>
            If a whole chain is compressed into one repeat unit, how much property variance becomes
            unexplainable — and does that share shrink when the data grows tenfold?
        </Text>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 40, marginTop: 34 }}>
        {[
            ['01', 'It reframes a decade of data', 'If Λ is positive and κ is near zero, the field has been buying interpolation accuracy inside its measured distribution — not chain physics.'],
            ['02', 'It is not a sampling story', 'A gap that survives a tenfold increase in data behaves like a missing coordinate. More data is then the wrong remedy.'],
            ['03', 'It is decidable with what exists', 'One Λ per (task, arm) cell, one slope per dataset. No new measurement, no new synthesis.'],
        ].map(([idx, head, body]) => (
            <Box key={idx} style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column' }}>
                <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 1.6 }}>{idx}</Text>
                <Text style={{ fontSize: 21, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', marginTop: 8, lineHeight: 1.3 }}>{head}</Text>
                <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#C3D0E2', marginTop: 10, lineHeight: 1.5 }}>{body}</Text>
            </Box>
        ))}
    </Box>

    <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#93A8C2', marginTop: 26, lineHeight: 1.4 }}>
        None of the four course topics covers organic or polymer materials — and polymer is the largest material class by production volume.
    </Text>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', marginTop: 'auto' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>Group 32 · How Much Is a Chain Worth?</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>4 / 18</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
